# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hand Cricket — Frontend Environment Variables
#
# HOW TO USE
# ──────────
# Local dev  : leave both vars empty (or don't create this file).
#              The Vite dev proxy handles /api and /ws automatically.
#
# Vercel prod: In your Vercel project go to:
#              Settings → Environment Variables → Add
#
#              Set BOTH variables below — replace YOUR-RENDER-APP with the
#              actual subdomain shown on your Render service dashboard.
#
# ⚠️  IMPORTANT — include the /api and /ws path suffixes exactly as shown.
#     Do NOT add a trailing slash.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# REST API base URL — should end with /api (appended automatically if missing).
# Example: https://hand-cricket-api.onrender.com/api
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://YOUR-RENDER-APP.onrender.com/api

# WebSocket base URL — should end with /ws, use wss:// (not https://).
# (The /ws suffix is appended automatically if missing.)
# Example: wss://hand-cricket-api.onrender.com/ws
VITE_WS_BASE_URL=wss://YOUR-RENDER-APP.onrender.com/ws
